# Cloud Deployment

## Reference platform
Google Cloud Run (but containerised — runs on any container platform: ECS, Fly, Kubernetes).

## Services
| Service | Platform | Spec | Port |
|---|---|---|---|
| Backend (server) | Cloud Run | 4Gi / 2CPU | 8080 |
| Worker | Cloud Run (different entrypoint) | 2Gi / 1CPU | — |
| Frontend | Cloud Run (or static CDN target) | Next.js standalone | 8080 |
| Database | Cloud SQL Postgres 16 | TimescaleDB + pgvector | — |
| Cache/Queue | Memorystore Redis | — | 6379 |

Worker entrypoint: `arq dqt_server.worker.WorkerSettings`.

## Database
Cloud SQL Postgres 16 with TimescaleDB and pgvector extensions enabled. Pool: 10 / 40 overflow. Private access via VPC connector.

## Secrets
Secret Manager prefix `dqt-*`:
- `dqt-database-url`
- `dqt-jwt-signing-key`
- `dqt-anthropic-api-key`
- `dqt-creds-key` (for warehouse credential encryption)
- `dqt-warehouse-credentials-{source_id}` (per source, generated at creation time)

## Edge routing
Load balancer routes:
- `/api/*` → server service
- `/ws/*` → server service (WebSocket)
- Everything else → frontend service

Static assets served via CDN.

## Setup and deployment
```bash
./setup/cloud/google-cloud-setup.sh    # first time only
./deployment/cloud/deploy.sh           # manual rollout
```

## CI/CD (GitHub Actions)
On every push to `main`:
1. Install (uv sync + pnpm install)
2. Lint (ruff + mypy + eslint + tsc)
3. Unit + integration tests
4. Build Docker images
5. Run DB migrations (`alembic upgrade head`)
6. Deploy server + worker + frontend

On tags matching `dqt-v*`:
- Publish `packages/dqt` to PyPI
- Publish `packages/dqt-cli` to PyPI

## Library publishing
```bash
git tag dqt-v0.1.0
git push origin dqt-v0.1.0
# CI publishes to PyPI automatically
```

## Environment variables in production
Set via Cloud Run environment or Secret Manager mounts. Never bake secrets into the image. Use `local.env` template as reference for required vars.
